WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.869
-Welcome back.
-It's good to be back.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.503
What a nice --
What a nice audience.

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:05.672
-It's a lovely audience.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.573
I think we're all equally
excited you're here.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:08.607
And congratulations.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:10.043
Since the last time
you were here,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.111
you won an Emmy for "Barry"
and a Peabody Award.

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:13.312
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.081
It's really exciting.
-Yeah, thank you, man.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.816
-And you were actually
in the building.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.651
You were doing Willie Geist's
show today.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.386
-Yeah, I was.
-Doing press for "Barry."

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:23.189
And you got -- this is very --
never happened before.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.223
-No.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:25.892
-You used to play
Keith Morrison on "SNL."

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.127
-I used to play
Keith Morrison on "SNL,"

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.864
the "Dateline" guy,
who's one of my personal heroes.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.465
-Yeah.
-He makes me laugh.

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.000
I don't know if you know him.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.136
He likes to do -- tell
terrible true-crime stories

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:39.038
in a very singsong kind of way.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:39.939
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:40.707
Ah, well.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.607
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:43.576
Yeah, so --
-So you met him!

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.112
-I met him today!
-You finally met him.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.314
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:52.385
-And I was -- it was like
the Beatles, and I was like --

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.787
[ Screaming ]

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:56.322
Yeah, I was freaking out.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.758
-Was he --
Does he like the impression?

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.193
-I hope so.
-Yeah.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:03.496
-Yeah, I go, "I hope you --
Did you like the impression?"

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.598
He went, "Ah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.034
Yeah, no.
It was very good, very good."

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:10.536
And then, yeah,
yeah, but I was nervous.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.805
I hope he --
But he was very sweet. Yeah.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.039
-That's great.

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:16.342
And then you were back at "SNL"
earlier this year

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.111
when our friend John Mulaney
hosted.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.512
-Yeah.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.113
-Is it fun to go back and do
a little cameo on the show?

00:01:21.113 --> 00:01:22.982
-Yeah. No, it was a blast.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.417
It was so much fun.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.186
And like, you know,
it's just good

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.255
seeing everybody
and things like that.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.656
I mean, I was gonna go back

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:34.327
and just do
the talk-show sketch.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.428
-The game-show with --
-The game-show sketch.

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:37.630
And then they were like --

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.498
I was watching
the Michael Cohen thing,

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:41.634
and I saw Jim Jordan on there,
and I was like,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.402
"I'm gonna have to
play Jim Jordan."

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.571
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.472
-And then I showed up,
and Lorne was like,

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:49.675
"So, I don't know if you watched
the Michael Cohen,

00:01:49.675 --> 00:01:51.978
but there's a guy
right in your zone."

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.879
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.914
You know?
And I was like, "Great."

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.416
-One of the nice things is you,
of course,

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:59.518
when you come back
and do a cameo,

00:01:59.518 --> 00:02:02.154
you don't have to do
the crazy hours as much.

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:04.857
But one of the upsides
of the crazy hours

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:08.427
is the fun that you have at
like 4:00 in the morning.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:09.496
-Mm-hmm, yes.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:11.998
-You were recalling
a thing Fred --

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.000
Fred Armisen used to do to me.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.540
-Yes, Fred Armisen would --
He would mess with Seth.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.876
So, Seth was the head writer
when I was there,

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:26.179
and Seth worked incredibly
long hours.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.347
And Seth would get
very little sleep.

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:30.783
And so when Seth
would go home and sleep,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.252
Fred would just be like --

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:34.453
Around 4:00 he'd be like,

00:02:34.453 --> 00:02:36.255
"Hey, man, do you think
Seth's asleep?"

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:37.322
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:38.924
And I'm like, "Yeah."

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.626
So he would call Seth,

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.630
pretending that he was, like,
a morning, like, zoo-crew guy.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.130
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:50.570
And that -- So the bit was that
Fred was being interviewed on

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.573
a radio show, and he gave out
your phone number live.

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:56.542
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.478
-So you would hear -- he would
have you on speaker phone,

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:00.980
and you'd hear like, "Hello?"

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.850
And he'd be like, "Hey!
We're on with Mr. Seth Meyers!"

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.884
How's it going?"

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.853
And then Fred
would start apologizing.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.422
He'd be like, "Seth,
I'm so sorry. I am so sorry.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.424
I didn't know they were gonna
read it out loud on the air.

00:03:12.424 --> 00:03:13.993
I gave them your phone number."

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.628
And you're like,
"Wait, what is going on?"

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.029
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.732
We would all be dying laughing.
-Yeah, I was not happy.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.067
-And you were like --
then we'd hang up, like,

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.302
[Bleep] you, Seth. Bye."

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:25.738
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.573
-This is obviously a very --

00:03:27.573 --> 00:03:29.475
-[ Laughing ]
-Yeah.

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.643
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:34.079
I mean, look, I can look back
on it and laugh.

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:35.248
-But you worked so hard.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.983
You worked, like,
such crazy hours back then.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:40.786
-Yeah, Fred was -- like, Fred
could always find that time

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:43.389
where you were so tired and you
didn't want any nonsense,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.824
and he would come and bring you

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.559
such delightfully
crafted nonsense,

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.361
that you had to sort of
tip your hat.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.763
-Yeah, you would be like,
"No, that was great, man."

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.065
I remember, he had another bit
was that, people would always

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.934
bring us gifts after they would
host, remember?

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.435
-Yeah.
-So, like, someone would host.

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.104
You would get, like, cupcakes
the next day.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.506
It'd be like, "Melissa McCarthy
sent us cupcakes," or whatever.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:03.709
And I remember Fred would just
come in with like --

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:06.679
it would be, like,
a six-pack of Coke,

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.114
but, like,
four of them were missing.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:08.814
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.015
And he would be like,

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:11.317
"Hey, guys, look what
Steve Martin got us."

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:17.590
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.192
And then,
if something terrible --

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.392
Do you remember in pitch --

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:21.794
I'm sorry, in pitch,

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.329
if something really terrible
had happened in the news...

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.163
-Yeah.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.666
-...he would say Colin Jost --

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.868
So, he would pitch -- we would
go around the pitch meeting.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.336
Lorne Michaels would be like,
"Seth?"

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.570
And then Seth would pitch.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.206
And he would go around,
and we'd all pitch ideas.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:35.040
So, it was Fred,
and then Colin Jost,

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.443
and then if something terrible
had happened in the news, like,

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:38.777
I don't know --
-A tragedy.

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:40.213
-A tragedy.
-Yeah.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.248
-Like the guy raised a girl
in his basement or something.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.149
He'd be like,
"Hey, did you read the thing

00:04:44.149 --> 00:04:45.184
about the girl in the basement?

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.585
I think that's terrible,

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:49.255
but Colin wants to write a piece
about it. I don't know why."

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:52.057
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.692
Colin would be like --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:55.227
-He would also do it.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.562
-He would be so nervous.

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.531
-He would also do it with people
that definitely like --

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.900
the kind of host that definitely
didn't know who Colin was.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:01.867
-Yeah.

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:03.068
-So it would immediately
be like --

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:04.704
They'd be like,
"Oh, I don't like that man."

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.339
-I'm not gonna work
with him all week.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.640
-"I don't want to do his thing."

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.908
-Yeah, and Fred would be like,

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.009
"I don't know why he wants to do
a piece about that,

00:05:11.009 --> 00:05:12.712
but it's his thing.
You should ask him."

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.214
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.550
Colin would be like, "Uh..."

